          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP297 Calgary Varsity [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I couldn’t find the cap to the SW of here tonight for any amount of sweeping (or consultation of old logs), but this one at least was a very simple find at moonrise. TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="700268559">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-07-09T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP297 Calgary Varsity [FOUND]

It is critical to keep good notes when looking for the caps in this area as the names are often similar. Hopefully I am logging these appropriately. This one involved a short walk. Always nice when there is a marker post. My 4th cap of the morning. The sun is shining and there are a number of sand flies (?) flying around. Thanks for contributing to a pleasant morning. These caps are a special challenge.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684223402">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP297 - Calgary Varsity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, picking up ones we didn't get to earlier! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A busy day today and lots of walking, but a lot of fun!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; We definitely took the long route to this one, but I said since we hadn't done many long walks yet today, this was our difficult exercise so far! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; The geodog really enjoyed it too!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683869217">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2034047">Cachin8r</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP297 Calgary Varsity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eleventh of 12 today, #868. I was not sure where the best approach was for this one given all the valleys, so I parked along the ridge in Silver Springs. Turned out to be a pretty good guess. We enjoyed the walk. Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-Cachin&lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_8ball.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;r&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683846817">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP297 Calgary Varsity - It was a great day for walking in the park, we actually walked enough to wear out the dog! &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iron Phoenix and I spent the day continuing our Calgary and area capping spree. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
